Zero downtime and revenue in 90 days are our non-negotiables. Engineering is right that an outage destroys lead value, so they get their full $3,500. Marketing is right that demand drives the funnel, but $4,500 starves sales execution. Sales is right that conversions matter, but relying on heavy discounts isn't sustainable. We are splitting $3,800 to Marketing, $3,500 to Engineering, and $2,200 to Sales, holding $500 in reserve. Marketing will repurpose launch assets into sales collateral, and Engineering will support enterprise demos. On Day 30, the $500 reserve unlocks for Sales if they achieve 15 signed customers or Marketing if they exceed 500 qualified leads.
  Reserve: $500, released on day 30: Released on Day 30 to Sales if they close 15 paying customers, otherwise to Marketing if qualified lead volume exceeds target by 20%.
  Trade: Marketing ad assets and webinar content must double as outbound Sales collateral.
  Trade: Engineering will directly support Sales with custom environment setups for top-tier enterprise demos.
  @Engineering: Ensure zero public outages and maintain system stability during peak launch traffic.
  @Marketing: Deliver target pipeline volume and supply Sales with launch collateral.
  @Sales: Focus on closing early deals within 90 days using structured non-cash incentives.

Engineering keeps their $3,500 to guarantee zero outages. To resolve the objections, Sales moves to $2,500, gaining $300 funded by Marketing, whose base becomes $3,500. Marketing regains the missing $700 through the $500 reserve plus a $200 conversion bonus if they hit target lead volume by Day 30.
